  "question": {
    "text": "A solid spherical ball of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;is released from the topmost point of the shown semi-spherical shell. The track is sufficiently rough to enable pure rolling motion.&nbsp;The normal force between the ball and the shell at the lowest position&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0025_d94b8e63b034.jpg\" style=\"width: 194px; height: 144px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>mg</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> <mn></mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>9</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>mg</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>mg</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>mg</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0025_d94b8e63b034.jpg\" style=\"width: 194px; height: 144px;\" /><br /><br />From the law of conservation of mechanical energy,<br /><br />Final energy = Translational kinetic energy + Rotational kinetic energy<br /><br />Hence, Final energy =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>I&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>mR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />Hence, we finally obtain,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>mg</mtext><mfenced><mtext>R - r</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mtext>mv</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; .......(1)<br /><br />and&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>N</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>mg</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>mv</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>R - r</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;..........(2)<br /><br />Solving Eqs. (1) and (2), we get<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>N</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>mg</mtext> </mrow></math>"
  }
}